{"key":"92698d08a6fe29b4","source_file":"Potts Fi.json","source_id":2756,"source_url":"concordance-fierce-ppl-saevus","term":"Fierce","headwords":["Fierce","Fierce, To be","Fierceness"],"latin":["Saevus","Saevire","Saevitia"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Fierce"],"latin":["Saevus"]},{"english":["Fierce, To be"],"latin":["Saevire"]},{"english":["Fierceness"],"latin":["Saevitia"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","HH","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6667","subsection":null},"text":"With rigour = unmercifulness. AC 6671.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"7272","subsection":null},"text":"Although they have lived in hatreds, revenges, rapine, in fierceness, etc.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"7370","subsection":null},"text":"Such at last love to be fierce with the neighbour. AC 9434:3.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9348","subsection":"7"},"text":"The delight of fierceness; nay, of cruelty...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"10618","subsection":"2"},"text":"All evil has in itself enmity, hatred, revenge, and fierceness...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"220","subsection":null},"text":"They are fierce against those who do not favour them. HH 481:5. HH 508:2. HH 573:2.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"290","subsection":"2"},"text":"Inwardly they blaze with... fiercenesses, etc. HH 380:end. HH 553. SE 5645:end.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"573","subsection":null},"text":"So great is the cupidity of being fierce against them.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"574","subsection":"2"},"text":"After the infestations they begin to rage against him with penalties.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"HH","section":"587","subsection":"3"},"text":"Their greatest delight is to exercise fierceness. HH 595:end.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"405","subsection":"3"},"text":"The evils of those who are in the love of dominion from the love of self are... fierceness, cruelty, etc.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"401","subsection":"12"},"text":"The day of Jehovah, cruel... ().","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"fierce-92698d","url":"/meta/potts/fierce-92698d/"}